; exec_baseline — SBPL allows that let posix_spawn of a
; libSystem-dynamic helper succeed under (deny default).
;
; Empirically derived against tests/suites/runner_use_c_worker/
; exec_fixture/helper.c on:
;   ProductName:    macOS
;   ProductVersion: 14.8.3
;   BuildVersion:   23J220
;   uname -r:       23.6.0  (Darwin 23.x is macOS 14 / Sonoma)
;
; See runner/augments/README.md → "exec_baseline derivation
; transcript" for the candidate rules, removal matrix, and
; re-verification recipe on a new macOS revision.
;
; NOT A NARROW BASELINE. (allow file-read*) is unconditional and
; covers EVERY path the worker can read. The augment was kept broad
; on purpose: the kernel reads the target binary's bytes before
; exec, dyld reads from /usr/lib + the shared cache + (sometimes)
; the binary's adjacent dylibs, and callers pass helper paths from
; anywhere on disk. Narrowing file-read* by subpath would force
; callers to standardize helper locations, which breaks the
; case-work tier's "helpers can be wherever you build them"
; promise. The cost: this augment cannot be composed with
; specimens that probe file-read denial. See README → composition.
;
; Append-only / allow-only contract: callers opting into this
; augment via `policy.augments: ["exec_baseline"]` consent to
; having these operations allowed even if their own source denied
; them. SBPL is last-match-wins and augments are appended after
; the caller's source.

(allow process-exec*)
(allow process-fork)
(allow file-read*)
